                    },
                    "message": "if this is only available after Erase is done, then we either need to check the status of the operation. But if the Erase is synchronous then it should just return this after. We can either have a new method that does that or something else."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item/Volume.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 88,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Wedig",
                        "email": "johnwedig@google.com",
                        "username": "johnwedig"
                    },
                    "message": "I added a new method called EraseByteRange(), which returns the number of bytes that got erased. It would only support those erase types where a byte range makes sense. Let me know what you think."
